    {
        q: "What is Spain's Crea y Crece e-invoicing mandate?",
        a: [
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "Crea y Crece refers to Spain's mandatory B2B e-invoicing framework introduced under Law 18/2022 and developed through Royal Decree 238/2026. It requires in-scope businesses to issue, send and receive structured electronic invoices for relevant B2B transactions with businesses or professionals established in Spain.",
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        q: "What formats are accepted for B2B e-invoicing in Spain?",
        a: [
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "UBL, Facturae, CII, and EDIFACT are all accepted syntaxes for invoice exchange. Peppol BIS is also valid on private platforms as it uses UBL/EN16931. All formats must conform to the EN16931 semantic data model.",
            },
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "Businesses using a private platform must also transmit a faithful copy (copia fiel) of every invoice in UBL syntax to the AEAT public solution simultaneously with issuance.",
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        q: "Does Spain require AEAT clearance before an invoice reaches the buyer?",
        a: [
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "No. Spain's model is post-audit, not clearance-based. Invoices are issued directly to buyers via accredited private platforms or the AEAT public solution. AEAT receives the copia fiel simultaneously but does not need to approve the invoice before it reaches the buyer.",
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        q: "What happens if AEAT updates its technical specifications?",
        a: [
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "ClearTax's compliance engine updates automatically when AEAT publishes new requirements- including the ongoing evolution of the Crea y Crece public platform. You don't need to track BOE bulletins or run emergency development cycles.",
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        q: "Does SII compliance exempt a business from Crea y Crece?",
        a: [
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "No. SII and Crea y Crece have different purposes. SII concerns VAT record reporting to the AEAT, while Crea y Crece governs structured B2B invoice exchange and related reporting. A business already under SII must independently assess its obligations under Crea y Crece.",
            },
        ],
    },
    {
        q: "What are the penalties for non-compliance?",
        a: [
            {
                kind: "p",
                html: "Non-certified billing software under Verifactu can trigger fines of up to €50,000 per fiscal year. Failures to issue or accept structured B2B invoices under Crea y Crece can result in penalties up to €10,000 per infraction. Invoice errors carry fines of 1–2% of transaction value, up to 75% in suspected fraud cases.",
            },
        ],
    },
];
